==English==

===Noun===
{{en-noun|-}}

# [[absence|Absence]] of [[responsibility]] for a [[crime]].
#: ''Her attorney managed to convince the jury of her '''innocence'''.''
# [[lack|Lack]] of [[understanding]] about sensitive subjects such as sexuality and crime.
#: ''In his '''innocence''', he offered the stranger to bring the package to Paris, never suspecting it contained drugs.''
# [[lack|Lack]] of [[ability]] or [[intention]] to [[harm]] or damage.
#: ''Tests have demonstrated the '''innocence''' of this substance.''

====Antonyms====
* {{sense|absence of responsibility for a crime}} [[guilt]]
* {{sense|ability to harm}} [[harmfulness]]

====Synonyms====
* {{sense|sensitive subjects}} [[naivety]]
* {{sense|ability to harm}} [[harmlessness]]
* {{sense|freedom from guilt}} [[unguilt]], [[unguiltness]]

====Related terms====
* [[innocent]]

